A checkbox's and a toggle's `@change(checked bool)` hands its handler the
control's state after the flip, on every target.

Both were once declared with a payload whose `value` is a string no host has
for an on/off control, so `e.value` was whatever each target happened to
spell. The parameter is now each host's own answer, which each override reads
and hands on: `e.currentTarget.checked`, fyne's `OnChanged(b bool)`, gtk4's
`gtk_check_button_get_active` and `gtk_switch_get_active` on the widget its
signal fired on, Compose's `onCheckedChange` argument, and on bubbletea the
override's own `!checked`.

The override writes `checked` from that same value before it hands it on, and
the write is the bound `:checked`'s write-back, so the binding reads what the
host reported rather than toggling. A toggle assumed the event fires once per
user flip, and fyne's `SetChecked` inside the box's own `OnChanged` fired it
again, flipping the bound var back and forth until the stack ran out.
bubbletea is the target with no host state to report, so its override flips
`checked` once and hands on what it now holds: computed twice, the write-back
flipped the var and the handler's value flipped it back.

gtk4's switch reports a flip only through GObject's `notify::active`, whose
callback is `(instance, pspec, user_data)`, so `sngl_connect` takes a second
trampoline for a notification. Before it the toggle was wired to nothing.

A test drives each through the platform's input path, handing the state where
the host would have it: onto the element on html, into the widget's state on
gtk4 (setting it is what fires the signal), into the callback on fyne.
bubbletea and android press the key and click the control, which flips it
whatever the test passed, so the test flips from the state it is in.

deny * `\bToggleEvent\b` -- the handler is handed the state itself, not a struct holding it
deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `bool\(C\.` -- a gboolean is C.int, which Go converts to no bool
deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `\be\.` -- the state is read where the press is handled; no event reaches the key case
-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import . "sngl:test"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
        fyne
        gtk4
        html
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
    none {
        html
    }
}

component main node {
    var on = false
    var lit = false
    var seen = "none"
    vbox {
        checkbox #box(:checked=on, label="a", @change(e) { seen = "box {e} {on}" })
        toggle #sw(checked=lit, label="b", @change(e) {
            lit = e
            seen = "sw {e}"
        })
        text(value=seen)
    }
}

func testCheckboxCarriesChecked(t Test, c main) {
    c.box.change(true)
    t.assert(c.seen == "box true true")
    t.assert(c.on == true)
    c.box.change(false)
    t.assert(c.seen == "box false false")
    t.assert(c.on == false)
}

func testToggleCarriesChecked(t Test, c main) {
    c.sw.change(true)
    t.assert(c.seen == "sw true")
    t.assert(c.lit == true)
    c.sw.change(false)
    t.assert(c.seen == "sw false")
    t.assert(c.lit == false)
}

window {
    main
}
